BQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"1d8837ff17121a258053d22c75acc6bfcc933208fe95edf20e5c1e16101824b3","event_uuid":"fa6f3e2d-e6cc-4da8-9f27-c4069ef616fc","position":{"commit_sha":"8bf78f330a2431629f0a3d40b2defc5a31699991","position":"1794374745901546306-fa6f3e2d-e6cc-4da8-9f27-c4069ef616fc"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Progress 2026-11-10 PST (session 3d705fec): plan revised per first review's BLOCK (wrong Cloud field-list test; added snapshot schema, payload round-trip and suppression-count details); second review PASS, certified at 02e86fe67db; claimed. Implemented as commit ec4f0bba399 in .rebar/worktrees/fixver-epic. Release suppression is wired through _build_outbound_context (release_adds/release_removes) per the review's advisory, ready for the outbound child. 6260 reconciler+interface tests pass; lint (incl. complexity + mechanism ratchets) and typecheck clean. make verify running (outside the sandbox).","timestamp":1794370278417951021},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Completion evidence 2026-11-10 21:20 PST (session 3d705fec):\n- Landed: Gerrit change 3345 submitted via scripts/gerrit_safe_submit.py at reviewed revision ec4f0bba3994c69a51da6abe977dba8f97ade6b0 with LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, 0 unresolved; merged on main as ed6ba4c4e9b5bfb895eb6b38a4fe70bbe56f43f0.\n- `env -u JIRA_URL -u JIRA_USER -u JIRA_API_TOKEN make verify` on the pushed commit ec4f0bba399 (20:11-20:45 PST): exit 0 — default tier 20932 passed / 29 skipped, integration tier 202 passed / 2 skipped. Log: .rebar/worktrees/fixver-epic/.rebar/scratch/3d705fec/make-verify-c3.log.\n- On merged HEAD ed6ba4c4e9b: `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` exit 0 (active=27 new=0 increased=0); `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` exit 0; largest src/rebar file is 799 lines (_ref_lock.py, untouched).\n- Gerrit's Verified +1 is the CI run of the same lint + typecheck + test contract.","timestamp":1794374347471557873},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"HANDOFF STATE 2026-11-10 21:23 PST (session 3d705fec): CLOSED. Gerrit 3345 landed (LLM-Review +1 / Verified +1 / 0 unresolved, safe-submit at ec4f0bba3994c69a51da6abe977dba8f97ade6b0), merged on main as ed6ba4c4e9b5bfb895eb6b38a4fe70bbe56f43f0. First close attempt failed only on missing recorded evidence for the ratchet/verify criteria; evidence comment added, second close passed.","timestamp":1794374745901546306}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1794256406426801001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"d9a605d5-e8f9-4988-813a-32312ffaa115","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"3a2b-a8db-d642-44ab"},{"link_uuid":"97f80c63-633f-487f-934b-696ee5fb0f61","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"701c-cd89-28a2-4b1d"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nrebar now stores `releases` (RELEASE_DELTA, schema v6), but the bridge never reads Jira's `fixVersions`: the Cloud search requests a fixed field list without it (`src/rebar/reconciler/adapters/jira/acli.py:238-251`), no inbound differ compares it, and no applier writes it. This child implements Jira→rebar per ADR 0124 (decisions 3, 4, 7), following the labels→tags path.\n\n## Approach\n\n1. **Snapshot contract first.** Add an optional `fixVersions` property to `src/rebar/schemas/jira_snapshot_entry.schema.json` (array of objects with optional string `name`; ABSENT means not fetched, so no removal is inferred, as with `issuelinks`), regenerate `src/rebar/types.py` (`python -m rebar.schemas.gen_types`), and add `fixVersions` to the consumer-read key set in `tests/unit/test_jira_snapshot_entry_schema.py`.\n2. **Fetch.** Add `\"fixVersions\"` to the Cloud search field list in `acli.py` (lines 241-250). Data Center needs no fetch change: its `search_issues` passes no `fields` (`adapters/jira_datacenter/_issues.py:199-205`), and pycontribs maps omitted `fields` to `[\"*all\"]`. The bound-but-absent GET (`acli_rest.py:325-333`) already returns all fields.\n3. **Diff.** Add `_diff_releases_inbound(jira_fields, local_ticket)` beside `_diff_labels_inbound` in `src/rebar/reconciler/inbound_collection_diffs.py`. It takes each version dict's string `name` from `jira_fields[\"fixVersions\"]` (skipping non-dicts and missing/non-string names), set-diffs against `local_ticket[\"releases\"]`, and returns sorted `{\"action\": \"add\"|\"remove\", \"release\": name}` records. Guard: if `fixVersions` is absent or not a list, return `[]` (mirrors the G1 guard in `_diff_link_removals_inbound`).\n4. **Mutation.** Add `releases: list` to `InboundMutation` (`inbound_differ.py:60-70`), compute it in `compute_inbound_mutations`, and include it in the emit condition. First extract the label-suppression block (lines 308-322) into `_suppress_collection_echoes(mutations, adds, removes, key) -> tuple[list[dict[str, Any]], int]`, called as `label_mutations, n = ...; suppression_count += n`, so the `bidir_suppressed` count is preserved. Carry `\"releases\"` through `run_differs.py` (inbound payload dict, lines 365-380) and add it to `InboundUpdatePayload`/`_INBOUND_UPDATE_KEYS` in `mutation_payloads.py`; `as_legacy_dict` always emits `releases`, as it does labels/comments/links.\n5. **Apply.** In `apply_inbound_events.py`, extract `_inbound_update_apply_labels`'s body (read state, no-op filter, add-wins dedup, reducer-failure skip) into `_apply_inbound_list_delta(...)` parameterized by payload key, entry key, state key and event type; call it for labels (`TAG_DELTA`, unchanged) and releases (`RELEASE_DELTA`), both writing `source=\"inbound\"`. Call the release applier from `apply_inbound.py` next to the labels call (line 133).\n6. **Contract.** Register `\"releases\": FieldSymmetry(name=\"releases\", symmetry=ADD_WINS, conflict_class=\"set\", outbound_name=\"fixVersions\", codec=\"Jira fixVersions[].name ↔ local 'releases'\")` in `_field_contract.py`, and `\"releases\": \"set\"` in `conflict_resolver.FIELD_CLASSES`.\n7. **Docs.** Add a \"Fix versions ↔ releases\" row to the sync-semantics table in `docs/jira-sync-setup.md` (\"Sync semantics & limitations\"): inbound supported, outbound in the next child, ADR 0124.\n\nImported tickets: the inbound CREATE path is unchanged; a ticket created from Jira gets its releases on the next pass through the bound-ticket update diff.\n\nSafety: no local writer of `RELEASE_DELTA` exists until the surfaces child, so the inbound set-diff cannot strip a locally intended release.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/schemas/jira_snapshot_entry.schema.json`, `src/rebar/types.py` (generated)\n- `src/rebar/reconciler/adapters/jira/acli.py`\n- `src/rebar/reconciler/inbound_collection_diffs.py`\n- `src/rebar/reconciler/inbound_differ.py`\n- `src/rebar/reconciler/run_differs.py`\n- `src/rebar/reconciler/mutation_payloads.py`\n- `src/rebar/reconciler/apply_inbound_events.py`\n- `src/rebar/reconciler/apply_inbound.py`\n- `src/rebar/reconciler/_field_contract.py`\n- `src/rebar/reconciler/conflict_resolver.py`\n- `docs/jira-sync-setup.md`\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/diffing/test_inbound_releases.py` (new)\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/mutate/test_inbound_apply_releases.py` (new)\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/test_field_contract_properties.py` (extend)\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/test_acli_search_pagination.py` (Cloud field list gains `fixVersions`)\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/test_dc_backend_characterization.py` (DC payload keeps `fixVersions`)\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/mutate/test_mutation_payloads.py` (round-trip carries `releases`)\n- `tests/unit/test_jira_snapshot_entry_schema.py` (consumer-read key)\n\n## Testing\n\nFixtures use the documented version shape (`{\"self\",\"id\",\"name\",\"archived\",\"released\"}`, Jira Cloud `Version`), since no production project has a version yet (ADR 0124 Evidence).\n- Diff: Jira `[{\"name\":\"2.4\"},{\"name\":\"2.5\"}]` vs local `[\"2.4\",\"old\"]` → add `2.5`, remove `old`; equal sets → `[]`; `fixVersions` absent → `[]` and `fixVersions: None` → `[]`, both with local releases present; a malformed entry (no name, non-dict) is skipped.\n- Apply: a release add/remove mutation writes exactly one `RELEASE_DELTA` with `source=\"inbound\"`; a repeat with state already matching writes nothing; a reducer exception writes nothing; with local releases not containing X, a mutation with add X and remove X writes `added=[\"X\"], removed=[]`. Existing label-apply tests pass unchanged.\n- Imported ticket: a ticket created by the unchanged CREATE path for an issue with fixVersions `[\"2.4\"]`, then one update pass on the same payload, gets one `RELEASE_DELTA` adding `2.4`.\n- Two passes over the same Jira payload: the first writes one `RELEASE_DELTA`, the second nothing.\n- Suppression: an outbound release add suppresses an inbound remove of that name, and the returned suppression count includes it; existing label suppression counts are unchanged.\n- Cloud search body `fields` includes `fixVersions`; a DC search payload with `fixVersions` reaches the snapshot with names intact.\n- Contract: `FIELD_CONTRACT[\"releases\"]` is `ADD_WINS`/`set`; `process_release_delta` keeps a name both added and removed in one event.\n- Payloads: inbound update round-trip with and without releases through `InboundUpdatePayload`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] A bound issue whose Cloud-shaped `fixVersions` gain a name gets one inbound `RELEASE_DELTA` adding it; pinned by the apply and diff tests.\n- [x] A DC-shaped payload's `fixVersions` reach the snapshot intact; pinned by the DC characterization test.\n- [x] A repeat pass with no Jira change writes no event; pinned by the two-pass test.\n- [x] A snapshot without a list-valued `fixVersions` never removes local releases; pinned by the absent and None diff tests.\n- [x] An imported ticket gets its releases on the following pass; pinned by the imported-ticket test.\n- [x] The Cloud search requests `fixVersions`; pinned by `test_acli_search_pagination.py`.\n- [x] `FIELD_CONTRACT` and `FIELD_CLASSES` register `releases` as `ADD_WINS`/`set`; pinned by `test_field_contract_properties.py`.\n- [x] Existing label inbound and suppression tests pass unchanged.\n- [x] `python -m rebar.schemas.gen_types --check` exits 0.\n- [x] `docs/jira-sync-setup.md` lists the fix-versions row.\n- [x] `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` exits 0.\n- [x] `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` exits 0.\n- [x] No `src/rebar` file exceeds 800 lines.\n- [x] `env -u JIRA_URL -u JIRA_USER -u JIRA_API_TOKEN make verify` exits 0 on the commit pushed for review.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/jira_snapshot_entry.schema.json","reason":"fixVersions snapshot key"},{"path":"src/rebar/types.py","reason":"regenerated JiraSnapshotEntry"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/adapters/jira/acli.py","reason":"fetch fixVersions"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/inbound_collection_diffs.py","reason":"release diff"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/inbound_differ.py","reason":"mutation field and suppression helper"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/run_differs.py","reason":"payload plumbing"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/mutation_payloads.py","reason":"inbound payload key"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/apply_inbound_events.py","reason":"RELEASE_DELTA writer"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/apply_inbound.py","reason":"call release applier"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/_field_contract.py","reason":"register releases"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/conflict_resolver.py","reason":"FIELD_CLASSES"},{"path":"docs/jira-sync-setup.md","reason":"sync table row"},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/diffing/test_inbound_releases.py","reason":"new"},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/mutate/test_inbound_apply_releases.py","reason":"new"},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/test_field_contract_properties.py","reason":"add-wins case"},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/test_acli_search_pagination.py","reason":"Cloud field list"},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/test_dc_backend_characterization.py","reason":"DC payload"},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/mutate/test_mutation_payloads.py","reason":"round-trip carries releases"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_jira_snapshot_entry_schema.py","reason":"consumer-read key"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["depends_on","3a2b-a8db-d642-44ab"],["parent","21ec-3e9b-4a27-4775"],["relates_to","701c-cd89-28a2-4b1d"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"21ec-3e9b-4a27-4775","parent_status_uuid":"19617d1c-3168-4a0a-b8bd-2e090a1eecdc","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"50aa-b7a1-e9a1-44ac","ticket_type":"story","title":"Sync Jira fixVersions into rebar releases (inbound)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["da04ba75-af71-40de-bd3e-beee6bf2c333","34493458-72dc-4e03-b0be-2bf94c73023a","efd025df-c897-454f-ab40-5da181a3d02c","27da156e-f900-44a5-a308-23118157a01a","b247df5b-8b98-43ac-977f-e27a6914cad6","648ea295-66e3-4332-b0ae-a428ef71fd6f","97f80c63-633f-487f-934b-696ee5fb0f61","1cfad7b1-d3d4-4aa5-b619-71e7c028344b","34b6a3d7-ded7-4e56-a0b0-478e657aa168","19617d1c-3168-4a0a-b8bd-2e090a1eecdc","38f83921-b9fa-4368-b65b-3b14f0df6fd5","fa6f3e2d-e6cc-4da8-9f27-c4069ef616fc"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794374745901546307,"uuid":"1483bfc1-4b84-4a6c-ba4b-0d1c394e5442